  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ethiopian Golden Age 1969-1974 Amha-Kaifa-Philips label canon — codified through Mulatu Astatke’s Berklee-and-NYC training brought back to Addis Ababa, the Roha Band and Walias Band as the canonical recording ensembles, Mahmoud Ahmed (Ere Mela Mela 1975), Alemayehu Eshete, Tlahoun Gèssèssè, and Tilahun Gessesse as canonical singers; characterized by Ethiopian kignit-modal vocals over jazz-and-soul instrumental beds",
